.SH NAME
niac-attachment-policy-list - List the policies in the policy file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac attachment-policy list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the policies in the policy file. Policies passed to the daemon as flags
are not in the file; 'GET /api/v1/attachment-policies' lists what the running
daemon actually approved. On Linux the package makes /etc/niac readable only
by root and the niac service account, so run it with sudo there.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  niac attachment-policy list
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-attachment-policy(1)\fP


